OL,3,GNEWSAAylesbury Estate's future
OL,4,Aconsidered by council
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn 1997, new Prime Minister Tony Blair
OL,7,Fvisited the Aylesbury Estate in south
OL,8,FLondon. Even then, the rows of
OL,9,Fcrumbling blocks of flats were in a
OL,10,Fsorry state.
OL,12,FBlair used it as the backdrop for a
OL,13,Fspeech in which he pledged to tackle
OL,14,Finner-city decay, saying "there will be
OL,15,Fno forgotten people in the Britain I
OL,16,Fwant to build".
OL,18,FAlmost 30 years on, most of the estate
OL,19,Fremains unchanged. The flats have
OL,20,Fdeteriorated and declined further, with
OL,21,Fmany now are abandoned and derelict.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
